00:32:21,032 --> 00:32:22,071
Do you want to join?

790
00:32:22,072 --> 00:32:23,572
(The fun run crew)

791
00:32:24,102 --> 00:32:25,572
I've heard that somewhere.

792
00:32:25,902 --> 00:32:27,042
Kian84 is disappointed.

793
00:32:27,242 --> 00:32:30,672
I'm sad that he has a connection with you.

794
00:32:31,412 --> 00:32:33,842
- He shouldn't be like that. - He's more of a fun run.

795
00:32:35,482 --> 00:32:36,652
Hello.

796
00:32:37,922 --> 00:32:38,981
(He says hello to children in a fun way.)

797
00:32:38,982 --> 00:32:41,052
That's how it should be. It shouldn't be stressful.

798
00:32:42,122 --> 00:32:43,921
- This is fun. - I know.

799
00:32:43,922 --> 00:32:46,922
- It's comfortable and nice. - I'm sleepy. I'm about to sleep.

800
00:32:49,432 --> 00:32:51,332
- Hey. - Oh, no.

801
00:32:51,962 --> 00:32:53,062
Oh, no.

802
00:32:53,702 --> 00:32:55,972
- Calm down, Na Ra. - I am calm.

803
00:32:59,902 --> 00:33:01,371
Your stamina is no joke.

804
00:33:01,372 --> 00:33:03,412
- You keep... - Of course!

805
00:33:04,682 --> 00:33:07,241
(He runs uphill.)

806
00:33:07,242 --> 00:33:08,982
You shouldn't overdo it when you have a fun run.

807
00:33:10,112 --> 00:33:12,122
You shouldn't go uphill when you have a fun run.

808
00:33:12,852 --> 00:33:15,691
- You would've eaten something. - I would've eaten something.

809
00:33:15,692 --> 00:33:16,852
I would've had takoyaki.

810
00:33:17,762 --> 00:33:19,092
(Eating)

811
00:33:19,362 --> 00:33:21,392
While I support the fun run,

812
00:33:21,862 --> 00:33:23,091
I think the records are important.

813
00:33:23,092 --> 00:33:25,102
(He doesn't disappoint.)

814
00:33:25,502 --> 00:33:27,332
It won't take much longer. We're nearly done.

815
00:33:27,532 --> 00:33:28,672
We're almost there.

816
00:33:28,872 --> 00:33:30,072
Run with your knees only.

817
00:33:30,332 --> 00:33:31,872
That's it. Run with that mindset.

818
00:33:32,072 --> 00:33:33,942
- Run with that mindset. - That's right.

819
00:33:35,012 --> 00:33:36,142
We ran 2km.

820
00:33:36,572 --> 00:33:37,981
- Did you say 2km? - Yes, we ran 2km.

821
00:33:37,982 --> 00:33:39,242
That means we're done.

822
00:33:41,952 --> 00:33:45,022
I thought that you'd get exhausted sooner.

823
00:33:45,652 --> 00:33:46,981
- I'm exhausted, Na Ra. - No.

824
00:33:46,982 --> 00:33:48,652
- I've been exhausted for a while. - No.

825
00:33:49,152 --> 00:33:51,121
What do you mean, "No?" I'm telling you it's true.

826
00:33:51,122 --> 00:33:53,162
You should run at least 3km.

827
00:33:53,492 --> 00:33:55,092
I was going to run 5km with you.

828
00:33:56,562 --> 00:33:58,062
You don't stop talking.

829
00:33:58,162 --> 00:33:59,732
Do you usually talk a lot?

830
00:33:59,902 --> 00:34:01,001
When I go outside...

831
00:34:01,002 --> 00:34:03,772
- You talk to other people. - Yes, I talk to other people a lot.

832
00:34:04,872 --> 00:34:06,202
I chat.

833
00:34:07,402 --> 00:34:08,641
We're nearly done. I'm serious.

834
00:34:08,642 --> 00:34:10,372
You just need to run a bit more. I'm serious.

835
00:34:11,482 --> 00:34:12,912
You're exhausted now, right?

836
00:34:13,582 --> 00:34:17,382
If you think of it in a broad sense, this is nothing compared to...

837
00:34:18,152 --> 00:34:20,082
the many things that are happening in the world.

838
00:34:20,952 --> 00:34:22,051
That kind of talk will make him lose energy.

839
00:34:22,052 --> 00:34:23,152
Enjoy it.

840
00:34:23,892 --> 00:34:26,022
- Why is there another uphill road? - It's okay.

841
00:34:27,222 --> 00:34:29,561
If I push you from the back, it'll be easy to go uphill.

842
00:34:29,562 --> 00:34:30,762
Really?

843
00:34:32,162 --> 00:34:34,201
(He runs with the exhausted Ryeo Un until the end.)

844
00:34:34,202 --> 00:34:35,932
Let's make a big circle.

845
00:34:36,902 --> 00:34:38,501
The number isn't clean.

846
00:34:38,502 --> 00:34:40,472
- You should run 4km. - We should run 4km.

847
00:34:40,672 --> 00:34:43,142
All right. We're nearly done. We just need 80m.

848
00:34:43,842 --> 00:34:44,881
We just need 30m.

849
00:34:44,882 --> 00:34:46,111
(Hands-on coaching to complete the race)

850
00:34:46,112 --> 00:34:48,112
We just need 20m.

851
00:34:48,382 --> 00:34:50,182
Cheer up!

852
00:34:52,022 --> 00:34:53,452
Okay. We're done.

853
00:34:55,992 --> 00:34:57,492
Well done. All right.

854
00:34:58,192 --> 00:34:59,262
Well done.

855
00:34:59,592 --> 00:35:01,631
(They ran 4km at a running pace of 10 minutes per kilometer.)

856
00:35:01,632 --> 00:35:02,862
Ten minutes per kilometer.

857
00:35:03,162 --> 00:35:05,962
Ryeo Un ran with me.

858
00:35:06,462 --> 00:35:10,132
I'm thankful for his consideration.

859
00:35:11,242 --> 00:35:13,041
- You said you were thirsty. - Yes.

860
00:35:13,042 --> 00:35:14,572
- Is that what he brought? - Yes.

861
00:35:14,972 --> 00:35:16,311
So that you wouldn't be thirsty,

862
00:35:16,312 --> 00:35:17,782
(He retrieves his shopping bag from the bush.)

863
00:35:18,042 --> 00:35:19,141
I brought a healthy drink.

864
00:35:19,142 --> 00:35:20,182
(What is it?)

865
00:35:21,782 --> 00:35:22,881
- Here. - Is it what he drank earlier?

866
00:35:22,882 --> 00:35:23,952
- It's what he drank earlier. - What's this?

867
00:35:24,052 --> 00:35:25,252
It's tomato juice.

868
00:35:26,282 --> 00:35:28,552
- How... - Just drink it from the bottle.

869
00:35:29,392 --> 00:35:31,992
(He drinks it from the bottle.)

870
00:35:32,292 --> 00:35:33,891
I packed one more, so drink it at home.

871
00:35:33,892 --> 00:35:34,991
- Thank you. - Okay?

872
00:35:34,992 --> 00:35:36,132
And open this.

873
00:35:36,432 --> 00:35:37,532
What is it?

874
00:35:38,062 --> 00:35:39,132
What is it?

875
00:35:39,762 --> 00:35:40,802
- What's this? - What's that?

876
00:35:41,002 --> 00:35:42,802
- The stickers from earlier. - These are ear seeds.

877
00:35:43,172 --> 00:35:44,401
They're amazing for removing puffiness.

878
00:35:44,402 --> 00:35:45,541
- Really? - Yes.

879
00:35:45,542 --> 00:35:48,542
Put them on before you get your makeup done,

880
00:35:48,912 --> 00:35:51,542
and take them off right before the shoot.

881
00:35:51,942 --> 00:35:53,112
Your puffiness will be gone.

882
00:35:53,812 --> 00:35:55,712
- I'll use them well. - Don't mention it.

883
00:35:56,552 --> 00:35:58,582
Doesn't it seem like a pyramid scheme?

884
00:35:58,822 --> 00:35:59,982
Your puffiness will be gone.

885
00:36:00,282 --> 00:36:01,752
I share things...

886
00:36:02,152 --> 00:36:03,651
with people I love.

887
00:36:03,652 --> 00:36:04,921
- You share things. - Yes.

888
00:36:04,922 --> 00:36:07,262
- Well done. - Okay.

889
00:36:07,892 --> 00:36:10,362
So, shall we run together next time as well?

890
00:36:11,262 --> 00:36:12,702
Let's run in spring.

891
00:36:13,032 --> 00:36:16,172
If you decide to run for real, I'll buy you running shoes.

892
00:36:16,632 --> 00:36:18,842
- He promotes running. - I know.

893
00:36:19,672 --> 00:36:20,842
I won't be able to accept those shoes.

894
00:36:24,342 --> 00:36:25,842
- All right. You did well. - All right.

895
00:36:26,212 --> 00:36:27,482
- Go. - I'll get going.

896
00:36:28,752 --> 00:36:30,811
(After sending Ryeo Un off, Na Ra runs by himself.)

897
00:36:30,812 --> 00:36:33,221
- It wasn't enough for him. - He takes long strides...

898
00:36:33,222 --> 00:36:34,621
- because he has long legs. - He's fast.

899
00:36:34,622 --> 00:36:36,152
(He runs fast.)

900
00:36:36,992 --> 00:36:39,562
The wind is blowing against me.

901
00:36:40,222 --> 00:36:41,262
It's cold.

902
00:36:41,592 --> 00:36:42,832
It suddenly turned cold.

903
00:36:44,292 --> 00:36:46,931
(He enters a place as he braves the strong wind.)

904
00:36:46,932 --> 00:36:48,331
- It's a gopchang place. - It sounds delicious.

905
00:36:48,332 --> 00:36:49,401
(A gopchang restaurant)

906
00:36:49,402 --> 00:36:50,502
Hello.

907
00:36:51,042 --> 00:36:52,502
Hello. Have you been well?

908
00:36:53,042 --> 00:36:54,472
Happy New Year.

909
00:36:54,612 --> 00:36:56,271
- Did you run here? - Yes, I ran here.

910
00:36:56,272 --> 00:36:57,941
- I was running. - Really?

911
00:36:57,942 --> 00:36:59,012
Yes.

912
00:36:59,442 --> 00:37:01,911
I came here because I wanted to eat tasty gopchang.

913
00:37:01,912 --> 00:37:04,851
- How nice. - You were on a diet earlier.

914
00:37:04,852 --> 00:37:06,322
Don't you do that for lunch?

915
00:37:06,522 --> 00:37:09,222
I make sure to eat one healthy meal a day.

916
00:37:09,352 --> 00:37:10,592
I also eat what I want.

917
00:37:10,792 --> 00:37:13,362
But in order to avoid eating at late hours,

918
00:37:13,662 --> 00:37:15,892
I move up my mealtimes.

919
00:37:16,232 --> 00:37:18,701
One serving of vegetable gopchang and one serving of fresh gopchang.

920
00:37:18,702 --> 00:37:19,931
One serving each.

921
00:37:19,932 --> 00:37:22,472
- Your regular order. - My regular order.

922
00:37:22,772 --> 00:37:24,472
Thank you.

923
00:37:24,902 --> 00:37:25,941
My goodness.

924
00:37:25,942 --> 00:37:26,942
(The regular customer orders quickly.)

925
00:37:28,772 --> 00:37:30,242
When I was little,

926
00:37:31,212 --> 00:37:32,812
I often went to the market with my mom...

927
00:37:33,242 --> 00:37:35,982
and ate vegetable gopchang.

928
00:37:36,112 --> 00:37:37,682
- Really? - Yes.

929
00:37:37,882 --> 00:37:42,221
This place has the most similar taste.

930
00:37:42,222 --> 00:37:43,222
(Chatty)

931
00:37:43,252 --> 00:37:45,261
I thought about which dish I ate...

932
00:37:45,262 --> 00:37:46,591
- the most often. - Yes.

933
00:37:46,592 --> 00:37:49,091
- This place came to my mind first. - Really?

934
00:37:49,092 --> 00:37:50,332
- Yes. - First?

935
00:37:50,592 --> 00:37:53,231
You're a chatterbox.

936
00:37:53,232 --> 00:37:55,132
I like to approach people first.

937
00:37:55,672 --> 00:37:58,042
When I was young, people often asked me,

938
00:37:58,772 --> 00:38:00,642
"Are you in a bad mood?"

939
00:38:00,942 --> 00:38:02,742
- So I smile a lot. - You have that face.

940
00:38:03,142 --> 00:38:05,012
When I smile a lot,

941
00:38:05,382 --> 00:38:07,951
I gain many opportunities to put other people...

942
00:38:07,952 --> 00:38:09,312
in a good mood.

943
00:38:09,512 --> 00:38:11,551
I told my actor friend about this place,

944
00:38:11,552 --> 00:38:12,981
and he said that he wanted to visit.

945
00:38:12,982 --> 00:38:14,792
- Really? - We'll come together sometime.

946
00:38:16,052 --> 00:38:17,491
- Gosh. - It looks delicious.

947
00:38:17,492 --> 00:38:18,561
(The gopchang is ready in no time.)

948
00:38:18,562 --> 00:38:20,022
- They're good. - It looks so tasty.

949
00:38:21,232 --> 00:38:22,791
Have a nice day. Bye.

950
00:38:22,792 --> 00:38:23,832
(He takes the food to go.)

951
00:38:24,432 --> 00:38:26,431
It should be eaten right away.

952
00:38:26,432 --> 00:38:27,602
I know.

953
00:38:28,672 --> 00:38:30,832
(Running)

954
00:38:31,642 --> 00:38:34,142
(He runs home before the food gets cold.)

955
00:38:38,842 --> 00:38:39,842
(My goodness)

956
00:38:41,652 --> 00:38:43,011
- What? - Packages.

957
00:38:43,012 --> 00:38:44,922
It was my birthday recently.

958
00:38:45,482 --> 00:38:46,952
- Presents. - So people sent me presents.

959
00:38:47,582 --> 00:38:48,692
For now...

960
00:38:48,822 --> 00:38:49,991
(He hurriedly takes his pajamas and walks over to the restroom.)

961
00:38:49,992 --> 00:38:51,261
I'll take these.

962
00:38:51,262 --> 00:38:52,292
(He hurriedly takes his pajamas and walks over to the restroom.)

963
00:38:53,592 --> 00:38:55,932
When you wash up and eat after exercising, it's a paradise.

964
00:38:57,192 --> 00:38:59,332
(Refreshed)

965
00:39:04,132 --> 00:39:05,341
- I mean... - He keeps doing that.

966
00:39:05,342 --> 00:39:07,142
His skin will erode from putting on so many products.

967
00:39:07,742 --> 00:39:09,671
He puts a lot of effort into his skin,

968
00:39:09,672 --> 00:39:12,482
- but his touches are rough. - Yes.

969
00:39:14,012 --> 00:39:16,452
(After moisturizing his skin with rough touches)

970
00:39:19,152 --> 00:39:20,152
It's time to eat.

971
00:39:20,153 --> 00:39:21,691
It'll be so tasty.

972
00:39:21,692 --> 00:39:23,922
(All right.)

973
00:39:24,052 --> 00:39:25,422
My goodness.

974
00:39:27,022 --> 00:39:29,532
(He plates his favorite gopchang dish.)

975
00:39:30,762 --> 00:39:31,831
Now...

976
00:39:31,832 --> 00:39:32,902
(Taking)

977
00:39:34,502 --> 00:39:35,571
Okay.

978
00:39:35,572 --> 00:39:37,272
- You use a pretty plate. - Okay.

979
00:39:42,772 --> 00:39:46,481
I'll eat it with lettuce.

980
00:39:46,482 --> 00:39:48,152
I read this somewhere.

981
00:39:48,412 --> 00:39:50,812
"When you make a dish for yourself,"

982
00:39:51,422 --> 00:39:53,421
"you can improve your sense of self-worth."

983
00:39:53,422 --> 00:39:55,651
- That's right. - That message made me think,

984
00:39:55,652 --> 00:39:57,652
"Those words are for me!"

985
00:39:58,222 --> 00:40:00,422
I think that's my influence as well.

986
00:40:00,592 --> 00:40:02,161
- You're right. - Really?

987
00:40:02,162 --> 00:40:03,262
Yes.

988
00:40:04,262 --> 00:40:07,361
(Cook84 cooks to improve his sense of self-worth.)

989
00:40:07,362 --> 00:40:08,632
It fills my sense of self-worth.

990
00:40:09,172 --> 00:40:12,342
When I eat in a pretty and cool way,

991
00:40:12,842 --> 00:40:15,972
it doubles my sense of self-worth.

992
00:40:16,312 --> 00:40:17,341
Okay.

993
00:40:17,342 --> 00:40:18,542
(Rummaging)

994
00:40:20,682 --> 00:40:23,411
(Pretty glasses for Na Ra)

995
00:40:23,412 --> 00:40:24,582
What? There are two.

996
00:40:25,452 --> 00:40:27,352
(Struggling)

997
00:40:30,122 --> 00:40:33,022
(He fills the glasses with long ice cubes.)

998
00:40:33,462 --> 00:40:35,562
(Opening)

999
00:40:36,032 --> 00:40:37,231
Then...

1000
00:40:37,232 --> 00:40:39,862
(What should I drink today?)

1001
00:40:41,002 --> 00:40:43,672
I'll drink this since I opened it.

1002
00:40:44,532 --> 00:40:47,102
My older brother is a distiller.

1003
00:40:48,272 --> 00:40:50,841
So he sends me samples to try.

1004
00:40:50,842 --> 00:40:52,782
(He pours the traditional liquor from his older brother.)

1005
00:40:53,212 --> 00:40:54,282
Coca-Cola too.

1006
00:40:55,982 --> 00:40:58,982
(He pours cold Coca-Cola in the other glass.)

1007
00:41:00,082 --> 00:41:01,082
Okay.

1008
00:41:03,552 --> 00:41:05,192
- Gosh, that looks so good. - That looks good.

1009
00:41:05,662 --> 00:41:07,861
It looks better than being in plastic containers.

1010
00:41:07,862 --> 00:41:08,862
Right.

1011
00:41:10,432 --> 00:41:11,462
Thank you for the food.

1012
00:41:14,602 --> 00:41:19,042
(Gulping)

1013
00:41:20,602 --> 00:41:21,612
(Groaning)

1014
00:41:22,612 --> 00:41:23,641
He downs everything.

1015
00:41:23,642 --> 00:41:26,381
- The first glass is always downed. - I love downing my drink as well.

1016
00:41:26,382 --> 00:41:27,482
The first glass is always downed.

1017
00:41:35,492 --> 00:41:37,051
My gosh.

1018
00:41:37,052 --> 00:41:38,322
He's eating it really well.

1019
00:41:39,062 --> 00:41:40,721
(Satisfied)

1020
00:41:40,722 --> 00:41:41,792
(Satisfied)

1021
00:41:42,162 --> 00:41:45,901
(He scoops it up with his spoon...)

1022
00:41:45,902 --> 00:41:48,771
(and eats it in one bite.)

1023
00:41:48,772 --> 00:41:49,872
He's eating well.

1024
00:41:50,402 --> 00:41:51,442
Right.

1025
00:41:52,942 --> 00:41:54,641
(A bite of the rice ball first...)

1026
00:41:54,642 --> 00:41:55,911
(and bite of the gopchang next)

1027
00:41:55,912 --> 00:41:56,942
This is it.

1028
00:41:58,842 --> 00:42:01,352
(Is it good?)

1029
00:42:06,452 --> 00:42:09,621
(He puts the glass noodles...)

1030
00:42:09,622 --> 00:42:13,392
(and gopchang into the wrap.)

1031
00:42:14,622 --> 00:42:15,662
This is what we live for.

1032
00:42:15,692 --> 00:42:17,131
I work out...

1033
00:42:17,132 --> 00:42:18,802
- to enjoy that. - Right.

1034
00:42:20,732 --> 00:42:21,732
(Letting out a breath)

1035
00:42:22,532 --> 00:42:25,102
(His sweat glands open.)

1036
00:42:27,842 --> 00:42:31,842
(He drinks the precious Korean traditional liquor.)

1037
00:42:36,582 --> 00:42:41,492
(He worked hard today...)

1038
00:42:41,622 --> 00:42:44,622
(and this is the reward for himself.)

1039
00:42:47,222 --> 00:42:48,292
I'll stop here.

1040
00:42:49,462 --> 00:42:50,462
Self-control.

1041
00:42:50,662 --> 00:42:53,302
It was because I had to perform the next day.

1042
00:42:53,532 --> 00:42:54,602
That's amazing.

1043
00:42:57,132 --> 00:43:00,142
(He turns around and puts down the spoon and chopsticks.)

1044
00:43:01,202 --> 00:43:02,511
(He cleans up efficiently from where he's sitting.)

1045
00:43:02,512 --> 00:43:04,841
It's easy to move around in a studio apartment.

1046
00:43:04,842 --> 00:43:06,241
- Right. - It's easy to move around.

1047
00:43:06,242 --> 00:43:07,382
Right. It's comfortable to get around the house.

1048
00:43:08,112 --> 00:43:11,422
(He skillfully captures the leftover food.)

1049
00:43:12,682 --> 00:43:14,582
(He spins it around...)

1050
00:43:14,682 --> 00:43:16,322
(and keeps it in the fridge.)

1051
00:43:18,892 --> 00:43:21,731
(After cleaning things up,)

1052
00:43:21,732 --> 00:43:24,492
(he takes the final sip.)

1053
00:43:27,132 --> 00:43:29,002
You should've had another glass with the leftover ice.

1054
00:43:30,502 --> 00:43:32,401
- Self-control. - I really wanted more,

1055
00:43:32,402 --> 00:43:33,402
but I stopped myself.

1056
00:43:33,403 --> 00:43:34,942
- You should have drunk hard liquor. - Right?

1057
00:43:36,842 --> 00:43:38,341
(He controls himself and brushes his teeth.)

1058
00:43:38,342 --> 00:43:40,542
- He never lazes around. - Right.

1059
00:43:45,052 --> 00:43:46,852
- All of a sudden? - To get rid of the dust.

1060
00:43:49,792 --> 00:43:52,322
I thought it was a restaurant ending the day.

1061
00:43:52,822 --> 00:43:54,462
That's how restaurants end the day.

1062
00:43:54,692 --> 00:43:55,862
"We're closing up now."

1063
00:43:57,762 --> 00:44:00,562
It was a day of consistency.

1064
00:44:02,972 --> 00:44:06,271
I believe it's important...

1065
00:44:06,272 --> 00:44:07,441
to fill the day with consistency.

1066
00:44:07,442 --> 00:44:08,471
- Gosh. - Gosh.

1067
00:44:08,472 --> 00:44:09,771
All of those things happened in that same place.

1068
00:44:09,772 --> 00:44:11,242
Right.

1069
00:44:11,612 --> 00:44:12,681
Doing things consistently...

1070
00:44:12,682 --> 00:44:14,582
all pile up.

1071
00:44:15,052 --> 00:44:18,122
Those things built up who I am now.

1072
00:44:20,152 --> 00:44:22,692
(It's time to rest for tomorrow's me.)

1073
00:44:23,952 --> 00:44:25,592
(Tapping)

1074
00:44:27,962 --> 00:44:29,432
(Jumping)

1075
00:44:31,662 --> 00:44:35,271
(A Person Called Na Ra Built by Consistency)

1076
00:44:35,272 --> 00:44:36,802
Gosh, that was great!

1077
00:44:36,972 --> 00:44:38,032
Thank you!

1078
00:44:38,772 --> 00:44:40,771
I could really relate to what you just said.

1079
00:44:40,772 --> 00:44:42,871
Doing things consistently all pile up...

1080
00:44:42,872 --> 00:44:45,042
to build up who you are.

1081
00:44:45,242 --> 00:44:48,181
It really reminded me to put that into practice.

1082
00:44:48,182 --> 00:44:49,681
He will wait for your comment the most.

1083
00:44:49,682 --> 00:44:51,521
- Bae Na Ra's role model. - Right.

1084
00:44:51,522 --> 00:44:52,522
Kian84.

1085
00:44:52,552 --> 00:44:54,322
Before a frog...

1086
00:44:54,682 --> 00:44:57,292
prepares for a leap,

1087
00:44:58,392 --> 00:45:00,762
there's a certain form it makes.

1088
00:45:01,762 --> 00:45:04,531
I think I've seen you say that on YouTube.

1089
00:45:04,532 --> 00:45:05,561
He's saying something he said elsewhere?

1090
00:45:05,562 --> 00:45:06,901
- He's using the same line. - Really?

1091
00:45:06,902 --> 00:45:08,831
He's using the same line he used elsewhere.

1092
00:45:08,832 --> 00:45:09,871
It wasn't even a great line,

1093
00:45:09,872 --> 00:45:12,102
- but he used it again. - We all prepare to leap.

1094
00:45:12,742 --> 00:45:14,501
- Leap? - Let's change it to "soar."

1095
00:45:14,502 --> 00:45:15,942
He was like a bird...

1096
00:45:16,472 --> 00:45:18,041
preparing to soar.

1097
00:45:18,042 --> 00:45:19,081
- Okay. - Right.

1098
00:45:19,082 --> 00:45:20,382
- A bird instead of a frog. - Right.

1099
00:45:20,412 --> 00:45:21,412
(I Live Alone)

1100
00:45:22,882 --> 00:45:24,581
(Cheer Up, Mr. Kim.)

1101
00:45:24,582 --> 00:45:26,022
"Cheer Up, Mr. Kim."

1102
00:45:26,682 --> 00:45:28,292
This place has changed so much.

1103
00:45:31,152 --> 00:45:32,521
(Dae Ho is standing in front of Cheongnyangni Station...)

1104
00:45:32,522 --> 00:45:33,821
(early in the morning.)

1105
00:45:33,822 --> 00:45:35,262
You're not going to meet your teacher, are you?

1106
00:45:37,992 --> 00:45:39,031
What time is it?

1107
00:45:39,032 --> 00:45:40,032
(Let's see.)

1108
00:45:40,302 --> 00:45:43,832
It's 9am. It's a tight schedule today.

1109
00:45:45,472 --> 00:45:46,841
It changed a lot.

1110
00:45:46,842 --> 00:45:49,212
- It changed so much. - Originally,

1111
00:45:49,312 --> 00:45:51,581
- there was something over here. - Isn't that Dae Ho?

1112
00:45:51,582 --> 00:45:52,742
Hey, Dae Ho!

1113
00:45:55,312 --> 00:45:56,312
- Who are they? - Who are they?

1114
00:45:56,313 --> 00:45:57,582
There are up to five men!

1115
00:45:58,322 --> 00:46:00,052
It's Jung Ho.

1116
00:46:00,422 --> 00:46:01,422
They traveled to Seoul.

1117
00:46:02,822 --> 00:46:03,991
It's his relatives.

1118
00:46:03,992 --> 00:46:05,521
(Dae Ho meets up with his relatives.)

1119
00:46:05,522 --> 00:46:07,392
- You're here. - It's great to see you.

1120
00:46:07,822 --> 00:46:11,732
Today, I invited my precious family members...

1121
00:46:12,062 --> 00:46:14,702
and cousins to Seoul.

1122
00:46:16,732 --> 00:46:17,771
(Dae Ho's family is famous for being a big family.)

1123
00:46:17,772 --> 00:46:19,401
- Right. - They are the cousins...

1124
00:46:19,402 --> 00:46:20,972
from back then.

1125
00:46:22,512 --> 00:46:24,042
(Has everyone come?)

1126
00:46:24,142 --> 00:46:26,742
(Look for those who are missing from your family.)

1127
00:46:27,112 --> 00:46:28,982
(A total of 10 siblings)

1128
00:46:29,612 --> 00:46:30,951
I asked each member,

1129
00:46:30,952 --> 00:46:33,621
and only these members could make it.

1130
00:46:33,622 --> 00:46:35,522
These many will gather...

1131
00:46:35,652 --> 00:46:37,051
for a great time.

1132
00:46:37,052 --> 00:46:38,621
- Many of them have come. - There are so many of them.

1133
00:46:38,622 --> 00:46:40,121
(They are planning to have a great time together.)

1134
00:46:40,122 --> 00:46:44,192
My eldest cousin, Kim Jung Ho.

1135
00:46:44,832 --> 00:46:45,861
Here you are.

1136
00:46:45,862 --> 00:46:47,761
(The icebreaker in the family)

1137
00:46:47,762 --> 00:46:49,801
He was the MC.

1138
00:46:49,802 --> 00:46:51,872
(MC Jung Ho)

1139
00:46:52,072 --> 00:46:53,672
My second eldest cousin, Kim Gun Ho.

1140
00:46:54,342 --> 00:46:56,911
Next is my younger brother, Sung Ho.

1141
00:46:56,912 --> 00:46:57,942
(Dae Ho's younger brother, Kim Sung Ho, 41)

1142
00:46:58,382 --> 00:46:59,981
- You just need to live there. - They look like each other.

1143
00:46:59,982 --> 00:47:02,152
(His younger brother with the exact same smile)

1144
00:47:02,352 --> 00:47:03,382
Kim Shin Ho.

1145
00:47:04,082 --> 00:47:06,181
My uncle's son. And Kim Sang Ho.

1146
00:47:06,182 --> 00:47:07,822
- All names end with "Ho." - He's the son of my youngest uncle.

1147
00:47:11,152 --> 00:47:12,391
(Sang Ho showed his dance moves for "24 Hours.")

1148
00:47:12,392 --> 00:47:14,222
That was when he just got out of the army.

1149
00:47:15,032 --> 00:47:16,062
Look at those moves.

1150
00:47:16,492 --> 00:47:18,301
As for Jung Ho,

1151
00:47:18,302 --> 00:47:20,801
he was handed over the family business in Yangpyeong.

1152
00:47:20,802 --> 00:47:23,871
He wasn't able to come to Seoul for around 20 years.

1153
00:47:23,872 --> 00:47:25,641
Even when he was busy with the restaurant,

1154
00:47:25,642 --> 00:47:28,042
he let us use part of his restaurant...

1155
00:47:28,542 --> 00:47:29,611
to have a cake ready...

1156
00:47:29,612 --> 00:47:31,981
along with different kinds of fruit.

1157
00:47:31,982 --> 00:47:34,941
He prepared the banner and birthday table for my father.

1158
00:47:34,942 --> 00:47:36,311
He prepared everything himself.

1159
00:47:36,312 --> 00:47:38,011
That banner is really touching.

1160
00:47:38,012 --> 00:47:39,122
He even prepared a banner.

1161
00:47:39,482 --> 00:47:41,792
He found a picture of my father when he was young.

1162
00:47:43,922 --> 00:47:46,392
(Thanks to Jung Ho who helped with the 70th birthday party,)

1163
00:47:46,722 --> 00:47:48,331
I will make sure to repay this moment.

1164
00:47:48,332 --> 00:47:51,391
(Dae Ho expressed his gratitude and promised to repay him.)

1165
00:47:51,392 --> 00:47:52,532
That was when I got that heart.

1166
00:47:52,702 --> 00:47:55,572
I wanted to thank my cousins separately.

1167
00:47:56,072 --> 00:47:57,772
That was how this occasion came to be.

1168
00:47:58,032 --> 00:48:00,971
Since my cousins all lived in Yangpyeong,

1169
00:48:00,972 --> 00:48:03,011
I wanted them to be away from that area...

1170
00:48:03,012 --> 00:48:04,971
and gift them a special day.

1171
00:48:04,972 --> 00:48:07,081
That was why I told them to come to Seoul.

1172
00:48:07,082 --> 00:48:08,411
To repay for their kindness,

1173
00:48:08,412 --> 00:48:09,612
- you prepared the Dae Ho Tour. - Right.

1174
00:48:09,852 --> 00:48:11,782
They feel like brothers.

1175
00:48:11,922 --> 00:48:13,582
- They look really tight. - Right.

1176
00:48:14,052 --> 00:48:15,091
Gosh.

1177
00:48:15,092 --> 00:48:18,051
Since Jung Ho helped out with my father's 70th birthday,

1178
00:48:18,052 --> 00:48:19,461
I thought it would be a good idea...

1179
00:48:19,462 --> 00:48:20,822
to spend a good time with the cousins.

1180
00:48:21,462 --> 00:48:22,592
- What will we be doing? - What?

1181
00:48:22,762 --> 00:48:25,062
Just follow me for now. That's all you need to do.

1182
00:48:26,132 --> 00:48:27,562
- What is all this? - Gosh.

1183
00:48:27,602 --> 00:48:29,331
How long did it take on the KTX from Yangpyeong?

1184
00:48:29,332 --> 00:48:30,871
Around 30 minutes?

1185
00:48:30,872 --> 00:48:31,872
Somewhere around 30 minutes.

1186
00:48:31,873 --> 00:48:32,971
- It's a quick ride, isn't it? - Yes.

1187
00:48:32,972 --> 00:48:34,871
- It's my first time here. - What?

1188
00:48:34,872 --> 00:48:36,671
- It's your first time here? - Is it your first time, Gun Ho?

1189
00:48:36,672 --> 00:48:39,082
It's my first time here in around 20 years.

1190
00:48:39,782 --> 00:48:41,441
It was his first time on the KTX.

1191
00:48:41,442 --> 00:48:43,151
- It was my first time on the KTX. - Really?

1192
00:48:43,152 --> 00:48:44,211
I'm serious.

1193
00:48:44,212 --> 00:48:45,821
It has been so long since the KTX has been around.

1194
00:48:45,822 --> 00:48:46,822
I didn't have the chance.

1195
00:48:47,052 --> 00:48:49,691
Dae Ho upgraded our seats...

1196
00:48:49,692 --> 00:48:51,051
to the business class.

1197
00:48:51,052 --> 00:48:52,092
Business class?

1198
00:48:52,762 --> 00:48:54,761
They're not called business class seats these days.

1199
00:48:54,762 --> 00:48:56,031
- Then what are they called? - Executive seats.

1200
00:48:56,032 --> 00:48:57,761
- Executive seats. - Executive seats?

1201
00:48:57,762 --> 00:48:58,932
- Executive seats? - Right.

1202
00:48:59,502 --> 00:49:01,402
I tried to sound better from the premium seats.

1203
00:49:02,272 --> 00:49:05,102
Hey, Sang Ho. Why didn't Seon Ho come?

1204
00:49:05,402 --> 00:49:06,771
He's taking a winter session.

1205
00:49:06,772 --> 00:49:08,511
Are you serious?

1206
00:49:08,512 --> 00:49:09,941
I've never missed out on any session...

1207
00:49:09,942 --> 00:49:11,372
after getting discharged from the army.

1208
00:49:11,782 --> 00:49:13,141
Same here.

1209
00:49:13,142 --> 00:49:14,442
You've taken all sessions?

1210
00:49:14,912 --> 00:49:16,852
I think it's colder here than in Yangpyeong.

1211
00:49:17,352 --> 00:49:19,122
It's colder in Seoul.

1212
00:49:19,522 --> 00:49:20,522
It feels colder.

1213
00:49:20,782 --> 00:49:22,651
- We met before. - We're here.

1214
00:49:22,652 --> 00:49:23,652
(They arrive somewhere through the chilly wind.)

1215
00:49:23,653 --> 00:49:25,962
All right, everyone. For today,

1216
00:49:27,522 --> 00:49:28,992
this will be our feet.

1217
00:49:29,192 --> 00:49:30,561
- What is that? - I rented a car.

1218
00:49:30,562 --> 00:49:34,862
(I rented a car.)

1219
00:49:35,672 --> 00:49:37,171
- Let's clap. - Gosh.

1220
00:49:37,172 --> 00:49:38,332
- Really? - Yes.

1221
00:49:39,742 --> 00:49:42,042
(Stay away, cold winter breeze.)

1222
00:49:43,372 --> 00:49:45,411
The Damarghini won't be able to move with all of those people.

1223
00:49:45,412 --> 00:49:46,481
Of course not.

1224
00:49:46,482 --> 00:49:51,011
I needed a mini-bus to drive a lot of people.

1225
00:49:51,012 --> 00:49:52,582
As it was a special day,

1226
00:49:52,952 --> 00:49:54,881
I wanted to make them...

1227
00:49:54,882 --> 00:49:56,952
experience something they have never experienced.

1228
00:49:57,052 --> 00:49:58,322
That was how I made my decision.

1229
00:49:58,662 --> 00:50:00,592
- Were you the driver? - I did the driving.

1230
00:50:00,962 --> 00:50:03,191
Jung Ho always drove around the cousins.

1231
00:50:03,192 --> 00:50:05,401
I wanted Jung Ho to feel comfortable today.

1232
00:50:05,402 --> 00:50:06,402
(Leave everything to Dae Ho Tour today!)

1233
00:50:06,403 --> 00:50:07,531
- Really? - We'll move around with this.

1234
00:50:07,532 --> 00:50:09,771
- You got us a bus. - I'll be the one to drive.

1235
00:50:09,772 --> 00:50:11,231
- Can you drive this? - I can.

1236
00:50:11,232 --> 00:50:12,601
- I didn't know. - I can drive this size...

1237
00:50:12,602 --> 00:50:14,001
with the Class One license.

1238
00:50:14,002 --> 00:50:16,411
It's around four times bigger than the Damarghini.

1239
00:50:16,412 --> 00:50:17,412
(Excited)

1240
00:50:17,413 --> 00:50:19,612
Let's hurry up and get on since it's cold.

1241
00:50:20,082 --> 00:50:21,741
- He went this far for this? - It's my first time riding this.

1242
00:50:21,742 --> 00:50:23,381
- I didn't expect this. - Gosh.

1243
00:50:23,382 --> 00:50:24,551
I'm riding a lot of new things.

1244
00:50:24,552 --> 00:50:25,552
It's my first time riding this as well.

1245
00:50:28,382 --> 00:50:29,591
- What? - What?

1246
00:50:29,592 --> 00:50:30,991
Did we get too surprised?

1247
00:50:30,992 --> 00:50:34,361
Inside, there will be water and snacks for you.

1248
00:50:34,362 --> 00:50:36,631
Make yourself comfortable and I will drive you all...

1249
00:50:36,632 --> 00:50:37,962
to the next destination.

1250
00:50:38,802 --> 00:50:40,461
- All right. - I see.

1251
00:50:40,462 --> 00:50:41,502
Gosh.

1252
00:50:43,602 --> 00:50:44,702
Gosh, it feels so dull.

1253
00:50:46,942 --> 00:50:49,041
With this sight, it looks like they will go to an Internet cafe...

1254
00:50:49,042 --> 00:50:50,741
and play a game of billiards.

1255
00:50:50,742 --> 00:50:52,481
They will then head home after a bowl of gukbap.

1256
00:50:52,482 --> 00:50:53,542
You're right.

1257
00:50:53,582 --> 00:50:55,351
How does a picture sound before we depart?

1258
00:50:55,352 --> 00:50:56,681
A picture? Okay!

1259
00:50:56,682 --> 00:50:58,552
(A picture sounds good.)

1260
00:50:58,622 --> 00:50:59,781
One, two, three.

1261
00:50:59,782 --> 00:51:01,681
We never had the chance to meet like that in Seoul.

1262
00:51:01,682 --> 00:51:02,892
- Right. - Everyone must feel excited.

1263
00:51:02,992 --> 00:51:03,992
- Great. - Aren't you the only one...

1264
00:51:03,993 --> 00:51:05,092
who is going to look good in the picture?

1265
00:51:05,462 --> 00:51:06,891
- Are you sure about this? - It is a bit hard to get everyone.

1266
00:51:06,892 --> 00:51:09,032
- Our faces will be in it, right? - I do see everyone.

1267
00:51:09,892 --> 00:51:11,491
- Let's go! - Here we go!

1268
00:51:11,492 --> 00:51:12,732
- Let's go! - Go!

1269
00:51:14,462 --> 00:51:15,732
How long does it take to get there?

1270
00:51:17,202 --> 00:51:18,472
I can't tell you that.

1271
00:51:18,702 --> 00:51:21,372
We can't even know where we're going?

1272
00:51:21,772 --> 00:51:23,271
Shouldn't we get at least a brief explanation?

1273
00:51:23,272 --> 00:51:25,171
Shouldn't we be told where we're going?

1274
00:51:25,172 --> 00:51:26,181
We don't even know where we're headed to.

1275
00:51:26,182 --> 00:51:28,581
Any tour would announce where we're headed to.

1276
00:51:28,582 --> 00:51:30,981
It's more fun to go somewhere without knowing about it.

1277
00:51:30,982 --> 00:51:32,351
We might not be told what we're doing there,

1278
00:51:32,352 --> 00:51:33,882
but we could be told where we're headed to.

1279
00:51:34,122 --> 00:51:35,692
That's the most exciting moment.

1280
00:51:36,822 --> 00:51:38,021
We're able to be in a car like this and travel around Seoul...

1281
00:51:38,022 --> 00:51:39,222
thanks to Dae Ho.

1282
00:51:39,562 --> 00:51:40,891
It was my first time riding the KTX...

1283
00:51:40,892 --> 00:51:42,262
and it's my first time riding a car like this.

1284
00:51:42,732 --> 00:51:43,792
Gosh.

1285
00:51:44,292 --> 00:51:46,402
All I have left now is getting on a plane.

1286
00:51:46,532 --> 00:51:49,602
Take your time to look around.

1287
00:51:51,872 --> 00:51:53,472
- The river looks great. - It's nice.

1288
00:51:53,642 --> 00:51:55,412
The river in Seoul feels quite different.

1289
00:51:55,772 --> 00:51:57,242
- Gosh. - The river in Seoul?

1290
00:51:59,412 --> 00:52:02,081
There are hand warmers, Sung Ho. There's gimbap as well.

1291
00:52:02,082 --> 00:52:03,581
There were things prepared for us.

1292
00:52:03,582 --> 00:52:04,681
- Gosh! - There's gimbap as well?

1293
00:52:04,682 --> 00:52:07,052
- Here's some gimbap. - Gosh, thank you.

1294
00:52:07,122 --> 00:52:08,592
- Dae Ho prepared a lot. - Thank you.

1295
00:52:09,092 --> 00:52:10,621
You prepared food for them to have in the car as well?

1296
00:52:10,622 --> 00:52:11,961
They had to come early in the morning.

1297
00:52:11,962 --> 00:52:13,022
I thought they would feel hungry.

1298
00:52:13,122 --> 00:52:14,421
The service is excellent.

1299
00:52:14,422 --> 00:52:16,162
It was still a tour I planned for them.

1300
00:52:16,792 --> 00:52:17,832
Great.

1301
00:52:18,662 --> 00:52:20,331
As I'm taking a bite, it happens to be beef gimbap.

1302
00:52:20,332 --> 00:52:22,432
- Right. - Right. It's expensive gimbap.

1303
00:52:22,802 --> 00:52:24,731
It's not regular gimbap. It's beef gimbap.

1304
00:52:24,732 --> 00:52:25,902
Gosh, it's good.

1305
00:52:26,102 --> 00:52:27,702
