1563
01:00:53,312 --> 01:00:54,482
but I'm really sleepy.

1564
01:00:55,412 --> 01:00:57,281
Two and a half hours was indeed long.

1565
01:00:57,282 --> 01:00:59,181
Of course. They traveled from Cheongnyangni to Incheon.

1566
01:00:59,182 --> 01:01:00,182
(While Gun Ho is fighting off sleep...)

1567
01:01:00,582 --> 01:01:01,751
- Is it here? - Yes.

1568
01:01:01,752 --> 01:01:03,122
(They enter the highway.)

1569
01:01:03,352 --> 01:01:04,822
I wonder where they're going next.

1570
01:01:05,292 --> 01:01:06,592
Traffic is getting heavier.

1571
01:01:07,462 --> 01:01:10,032
Is the second destination a secret as well?

1572
01:01:10,092 --> 01:01:11,362
Yes, it is, but...

1573
01:01:12,932 --> 01:01:16,472
When people went to do manual labor in the past,

1574
01:01:16,632 --> 01:01:18,132
they just hopped in when the van arrived.

1575
01:01:19,032 --> 01:01:20,802
You don't know where you're going and doing what.

1576
01:01:21,102 --> 01:01:22,172
Right. I've heard about it.

1577
01:01:23,572 --> 01:01:24,911
That's how it feels right now.

1578
01:01:24,912 --> 01:01:26,581
It does feel like they're being sold off.

1579
01:01:26,582 --> 01:01:27,982
Despite that...

1580
01:01:28,112 --> 01:01:30,412
I can only do this because we're cousins.

1581
01:01:31,882 --> 01:01:33,651
(Before they knew it, they arrived in Seoul.)

1582
01:01:33,652 --> 01:01:35,552
- We're back in Seoul. - Oh, you went back to Seoul.

1583
01:01:35,822 --> 01:01:37,292
How inefficient is that?

1584
01:01:38,352 --> 01:01:40,091
I don't know where we are, driving around like this.

1585
01:01:40,092 --> 01:01:41,222
- You can't... - Yes.

1586
01:01:41,922 --> 01:01:43,261
You can't tell...

1587
01:01:43,262 --> 01:01:44,562
- because we're driving, right? - Right. I can't tell.

1588
01:01:47,232 --> 01:01:48,301
You can see National Agricultural Cooperative Federation...

1589
01:01:48,302 --> 01:01:49,332
on your left, right?

1590
01:01:49,772 --> 01:01:51,101
This is where you claim your money when you win...

1591
01:01:51,102 --> 01:01:52,472
first prize in the lottery.

1592
01:01:53,442 --> 01:01:54,442
(Staring)

1593
01:01:54,443 --> 01:01:55,542
I should come here.

1594
01:01:55,912 --> 01:01:57,611
There should be an occasion for me to come here.

1595
01:01:57,612 --> 01:01:59,012
I have a ticket I haven't checked for this week.

1596
01:02:00,312 --> 01:02:01,812
I should get it exchanged.

1597
01:02:02,812 --> 01:02:04,681
- He's funny. - I should come here one day.

1598
01:02:04,682 --> 01:02:06,022
(Touching)

1599
01:02:06,282 --> 01:02:07,522
(Amused)

1600
01:02:07,622 --> 01:02:08,722
Are you checking it now?

1601
01:02:08,782 --> 01:02:10,021
- I... Before we set off... - You'd cash it in...

1602
01:02:10,022 --> 01:02:11,251
since you're here?

1603
01:02:11,252 --> 01:02:13,822
Yes, since I'm here. When else would I come?

1604
01:02:14,122 --> 01:02:15,462
"Potential 1.8 million dollars."

1605
01:02:16,692 --> 01:02:18,462
I think the second-prize winners cash it in here too.

1606
01:02:19,132 --> 01:02:21,262
Third-prize winners get a few thousand dollars.

1607
01:02:21,862 --> 01:02:23,431
Around 1,500 or 1,600 dollars?

1608
01:02:23,432 --> 01:02:25,371
It's between 1,000 and 2,000.

1609
01:02:25,372 --> 01:02:27,642
Right. That's why the third-prize winners should come here too.

1610
01:02:28,902 --> 01:02:30,972
Look at his face. Is his expression changing?

1611
01:02:31,972 --> 01:02:33,781
(Heart pounding)

1612
01:02:33,782 --> 01:02:35,642
- Go straight. - What?

1613
01:02:36,112 --> 01:02:37,152
We don't need to drop by.

1614
01:02:38,182 --> 01:02:39,521
- Should we just go? - Yes.

1615
01:02:39,522 --> 01:02:40,651
- Okay. - It's hard to win...

1616
01:02:40,652 --> 01:02:41,751
even five dollars these days.

1617
01:02:41,752 --> 01:02:43,222
(Upset)

1618
01:02:43,322 --> 01:02:45,351
You can only win five dollars if you have a lucky dream these days.

1619
01:02:45,352 --> 01:02:46,362
(Luck suddenly feels harder to come by.)

1620
01:02:46,462 --> 01:02:48,162
- You can't with just any dreams. - Exactly.

1621
01:02:49,062 --> 01:02:50,362
I can see Seoul Station now.

1622
01:02:53,162 --> 01:02:56,572
This is where all of us can relate to.

1623
01:02:57,002 --> 01:02:58,032
Relate?

1624
01:02:58,272 --> 01:03:00,772
I'm sure they're excited on the inside.

1625
01:03:00,902 --> 01:03:02,142
It's only starting.

1626
01:03:02,502 --> 01:03:03,942
What could it be? It is intriguing.

1627
01:03:04,712 --> 01:03:05,842
A hand warmer...

1628
01:03:06,342 --> 01:03:08,542
- Take a hand warmer each. - A hand warmer?

1629
01:03:08,912 --> 01:03:11,782
Are they doing something outside, since they're taking a hand warmer?

1630
01:03:12,052 --> 01:03:13,082
Have you all taken hand warmers?

1631
01:03:13,252 --> 01:03:14,482
- Yes. - Yes, we took one each.

1632
01:03:14,822 --> 01:03:15,991
- I... - I have it.

1633
01:03:15,992 --> 01:03:17,152
You must take it.

1634
01:03:17,622 --> 01:03:18,752
- Is it outside? - It must be outside.

1635
01:03:19,322 --> 01:03:20,422
We're doing something outside?

1636
01:03:23,562 --> 01:03:25,092
Dae Ho, go step by step.

1637
01:03:25,492 --> 01:03:27,432
- Dae Ho. - You're sweating, right?

1638
01:03:28,162 --> 01:03:31,272
(Making a fuss together)

1639
01:03:31,972 --> 01:03:34,472
We got to the ice rink in front of the City Hall.

1640
01:03:35,072 --> 01:03:36,271
(Set up in the middle of Seoul)

1641
01:03:36,272 --> 01:03:38,371
- That's a really famous spot. - It's really popular.

1642
01:03:38,372 --> 01:03:40,042
- In front of the City Hall? - Yes.

1643
01:03:40,282 --> 01:03:42,982
There was a small reservoir in the town.

1644
01:03:43,282 --> 01:03:44,652
When it froze hard,

1645
01:03:45,352 --> 01:03:47,182
we enjoyed winter sports there.

1646
01:03:47,682 --> 01:03:50,252
We went sledding on it.

1647
01:03:50,492 --> 01:03:52,352
Jung Ho always pulled by sled.

1648
01:03:52,792 --> 01:03:54,492
And Gun Ho pushed it from behind.

1649
01:03:55,062 --> 01:03:57,192
I have a memory of playing with them on the ice.

1650
01:03:57,492 --> 01:03:59,162
- I went sledding a lot in Yeoju. - Right?

1651
01:03:59,932 --> 01:04:02,671
It's a sled made of wooden planks nailed together, right?

1652
01:04:02,672 --> 01:04:03,832
- I used to ride that a lot too. - That's right.

1653
01:04:04,072 --> 01:04:05,332
We used a kitchen knife to sled.

1654
01:04:05,772 --> 01:04:07,542
- That's right. - A kitchen knife.

1655
01:04:07,772 --> 01:04:09,471
- One with a broken blade. - Right, with a broken blade.

1656
01:04:09,472 --> 01:04:10,641
- No way. - One with a broken blade.

1657
01:04:10,642 --> 01:04:11,872
That's right.

1658
01:04:12,612 --> 01:04:13,612
How do I do this?

1659
01:04:13,613 --> 01:04:15,682
I don't remember us skating together.

1660
01:04:16,352 --> 01:04:18,312
They're so cute. They're all going in a line.

1661
01:04:19,082 --> 01:04:21,222
- You said it'd bring back memories. - I know.

1662
01:04:21,422 --> 01:04:22,752
You said it'd bring back memories.

1663
01:04:22,892 --> 01:04:24,122
- You said it'd bring back memories! - Darn. Old memories...

1664
01:04:24,552 --> 01:04:25,652
Old memories...

1665
01:04:25,822 --> 01:04:27,722
- It's on your clothes. - No one can skate well.

1666
01:04:28,062 --> 01:04:29,261
No one can skate.

1667
01:04:29,262 --> 01:04:30,492
Why did you go there?

1668
01:04:31,262 --> 01:04:33,202
- To make memories on the ice. - For memories.

1669
01:04:36,402 --> 01:04:38,531
(Even the guide is a beginner.)

1670
01:04:38,532 --> 01:04:39,702
I'd never skated too.

1671
01:04:40,872 --> 01:04:44,011
(The Ho brothers are struggling on the ice.)

1672
01:04:44,012 --> 01:04:45,212
(Shouting)

1673
01:04:46,412 --> 01:04:48,581
(Flailing about)

1674
01:04:48,582 --> 01:04:50,012
Oh, no.

1675
01:04:50,412 --> 01:04:51,552
It was so hard.

1676
01:04:52,922 --> 01:04:55,122
(Falling here and there)

1677
01:04:55,922 --> 01:04:59,152
(They all fall together.)

1678
01:04:59,362 --> 01:05:00,661
- Would you be okay tomorrow? - Shouldn't he feed us...

1679
01:05:00,662 --> 01:05:01,962
before making us skate?

1680
01:05:02,422 --> 01:05:03,931
- Right. You should eat. - They hadn't had any food...

1681
01:05:03,932 --> 01:05:05,462
since they had gimbap.

1682
01:05:06,162 --> 01:05:08,032
Let's rest now. My goodness.

1683
01:05:08,902 --> 01:05:10,671
I should've taken tomorrow off too.

1684
01:05:10,672 --> 01:05:11,802
I know. This is bad.

1685
01:05:12,472 --> 01:05:13,472
(Sighing)

1686
01:05:13,472 --> 01:05:14,472
(Panting)

1687
01:05:15,472 --> 01:05:17,611
(Everyone is moaning.)

1688
01:05:17,612 --> 01:05:18,712
They're all about to die.

1689
01:05:19,142 --> 01:05:20,282
Still, it was fun.

1690
01:05:20,742 --> 01:05:22,681
- It was fun, indeed. - It was fun.

1691
01:05:22,682 --> 01:05:24,982
- They're satisfied. - Yes, they're getting satisfied.

1692
01:05:25,112 --> 01:05:26,721
- They're getting satisfied. - It's been long since I skated.

1693
01:05:26,722 --> 01:05:28,752
- You don't get to skate like this. - I know.

1694
01:05:28,952 --> 01:05:30,822
Let's go and have some snacks.

1695
01:05:32,352 --> 01:05:33,722
Order whatever you want.

1696
01:05:34,292 --> 01:05:35,361
There's fishcake. Yes.

1697
01:05:35,362 --> 01:05:37,431
First of all... One, two, three, four, five...

1698
01:05:37,432 --> 01:05:38,432
(A snack bar where Dae Ho will treat everyone)

1699
01:05:39,902 --> 01:05:41,531
You need a hot soup when it's cold.

1700
01:05:41,532 --> 01:05:44,202
(Fishcake and udon that'll warm you up)

1701
01:05:45,472 --> 01:05:47,501
(And the nation's favorite snack, tteokbokki)

1702
01:05:47,502 --> 01:05:49,102
Was it a build-up to eat that?

1703
01:05:50,112 --> 01:05:53,281
Shall we order about four servings of tteokbokki?

1704
01:05:53,282 --> 01:05:55,382
- Shall we have a fishcake skewer? - We must have that.

1705
01:05:55,582 --> 01:05:56,812
Let's order just two drinks.

1706
01:05:57,712 --> 01:05:58,982
- Thank you for the food. - Goodness.

1707
01:05:59,152 --> 01:06:00,322
Let's go.

1708
01:06:01,422 --> 01:06:03,351
- Thank you for the food. - Thank you for the food.

1709
01:06:03,352 --> 01:06:04,522
Enjoy your food.

1710
01:06:05,422 --> 01:06:07,791
(The long-awaited first bite)

1711
01:06:07,792 --> 01:06:08,792
(Exclaiming)

1712
01:06:09,762 --> 01:06:10,762
(Exclaiming)

1713
01:06:11,432 --> 01:06:12,591
(Taking a bite of the fishcake)

1714
01:06:12,592 --> 01:06:15,461
It tastes better after being out in the cold.

1715
01:06:15,462 --> 01:06:16,532
I know.

1716
01:06:19,602 --> 01:06:20,702
It's so good.

1717
01:06:21,372 --> 01:06:22,841
They're eating hurriedly.

1718
01:06:22,842 --> 01:06:25,511
(Eating hurriedly)

1719
01:06:25,512 --> 01:06:26,581
Put the noodles in here?

1720
01:06:26,582 --> 01:06:27,742
- Yes, in the soup. - This is good.

1721
01:06:28,642 --> 01:06:29,951
Everyone must've been hungry.

1722
01:06:29,952 --> 01:06:31,112
(Feeling bad)

1723
01:06:31,452 --> 01:06:32,612
Our memories...

1724
01:06:33,552 --> 01:06:35,952
Memories... I mean...

1725
01:06:36,122 --> 01:06:37,822
Is there another spot of our memories?

1726
01:06:38,552 --> 01:06:39,822
He's hoping there isn't.

1727
01:06:42,492 --> 01:06:43,762
What? There's one more?

1728
01:06:44,562 --> 01:06:45,792
What? There's one more?

1729
01:06:46,702 --> 01:06:47,831
You see?

1730
01:06:47,832 --> 01:06:49,432
He's checking, hoping there won't be.

1731
01:06:50,002 --> 01:06:51,402
- There are many spots left. - Oh, really?

1732
01:06:51,872 --> 01:06:54,342
Couldn't you share a little about our next destination?

1733
01:06:55,602 --> 01:06:57,241
The next spot we're going to...

1734
01:06:57,242 --> 01:06:58,572
(The next spot is...)

1735
01:06:58,872 --> 01:07:00,182
I bet you've never been there.

1736
01:07:00,682 --> 01:07:01,811
Can we not go?

1737
01:07:01,812 --> 01:07:03,382
(Joking)

1738
01:07:03,612 --> 01:07:05,412
The spot you've never been to.

1739
01:07:06,882 --> 01:07:08,982
(To the unexplored spot)

1740
01:07:09,952 --> 01:07:12,521
(Following without knowing anything)

1741
01:07:12,522 --> 01:07:13,622
What is it?

1742
01:07:14,122 --> 01:07:15,492
We're going uphill?

1743
01:07:17,832 --> 01:07:19,361
The climax was...

1744
01:07:19,362 --> 01:07:22,401
"How can I trigger their dopamine rush?"

1745
01:07:22,402 --> 01:07:23,672
I gave it a lot of thought.

1746
01:07:24,002 --> 01:07:26,942
"A place they can't even imagine. Where could it be?"

1747
01:07:27,172 --> 01:07:28,301
"What shall we do?"

1748
01:07:28,302 --> 01:07:29,302
(Where could that place be?)

1749
01:07:30,672 --> 01:07:31,742
My place.

1750
01:07:35,412 --> 01:07:36,482
Come in.

1751
01:07:37,312 --> 01:07:38,781
It's different from what I saw on TV.

1752
01:07:38,782 --> 01:07:39,882
(It's different from what I saw.)

1753
01:07:40,582 --> 01:07:42,252
- Let's go. Let's go in. - Welcome.

1754
01:07:42,782 --> 01:07:43,951
It's the beach!

1755
01:07:43,952 --> 01:07:45,121
(Daeundae unfolds when you open the gate.)

1756
01:07:45,122 --> 01:07:46,222
This is the beach.

1757
01:07:47,522 --> 01:07:49,861
(The ultimate dream, a home sauna)

1758
01:07:49,862 --> 01:07:51,292
I'm really envious of it.

1759
01:07:51,932 --> 01:07:53,631
(And a living mini-ecosystem, vivarium)

1760
01:07:53,632 --> 01:07:54,932
He really is an expert.

1761
01:07:55,532 --> 01:07:57,332
(The landmark of Mount Inwang)

1762
01:07:57,602 --> 01:07:59,001
It really is unusual.

1763
01:07:59,002 --> 01:08:00,172
He's a natural person.

1764
01:08:02,002 --> 01:08:03,472
I do want to visit it once.

1765
01:08:03,772 --> 01:08:05,112
- It's really interesting. - Right.

1766
01:08:06,812 --> 01:08:08,812
Oh, this is the beach you made.

1767
01:08:10,282 --> 01:08:11,552
It's a complete mess.

1768
01:08:12,552 --> 01:08:13,721
(The sand paradise is still there.)

1769
01:08:13,722 --> 01:08:14,822
Come in, everyone.

1770
01:08:15,152 --> 01:08:16,721
- Can I come in with my shoes on? - Yes, you can.

1771
01:08:16,722 --> 01:08:17,922
(Come in with your shoes on.)

1772
01:08:18,152 --> 01:08:21,191
When on earth are you going to get rid of the sand?

1773
01:08:21,192 --> 01:08:22,961
There's sand everywhere.

1774
01:08:22,962 --> 01:08:23,992
No idea.

1775
01:08:24,492 --> 01:08:27,802
This is the sauna and a bath.

1776
01:08:29,062 --> 01:08:30,902
It looks bigger in person.

1777
01:08:31,272 --> 01:08:33,001
I use the sauna really well.

1778
01:08:33,002 --> 01:08:34,442
I think the sauna is the best part of your house.

1779
01:08:35,372 --> 01:08:38,172
(Dae Ho shows the house around.)

1780
01:08:38,272 --> 01:08:39,812
This is like a greenhouse.

1781
01:08:40,612 --> 01:08:41,912
These are vivariums.

1782
01:08:42,482 --> 01:08:44,151
- I grow plants too. - Look at this.

1783
01:08:44,152 --> 01:08:45,651
It smells like mushroom.

1784
01:08:45,652 --> 01:08:47,151
Right. It's like a greenhouse.

1785
01:08:47,152 --> 01:08:48,182
Gosh, this...

1786
01:08:48,282 --> 01:08:49,722
- There's a lizard too. - There's a lizard.

1787
01:08:50,752 --> 01:08:52,792
Do you want to see the other house too?

1788
01:08:53,092 --> 01:08:54,661
- The other house? - Do we have to go out?

1789
01:08:54,662 --> 01:08:55,892
- No, we can go across from here. - Do we...

1790
01:08:56,232 --> 01:08:57,232
- What? - What?

1791
01:08:57,233 --> 01:08:58,331
We should check it out since we're here.

1792
01:08:58,332 --> 01:08:59,862
When else would we come back?

1793
01:09:00,462 --> 01:09:03,002
- Gosh, this is the roof. - That's right.

1794
01:09:05,532 --> 01:09:06,672
Be careful.

1795
01:09:07,172 --> 01:09:08,242
Earlier...

1796
01:09:09,272 --> 01:09:10,272
(Laughing)

1797
01:09:10,273 --> 01:09:11,371
Goodness.

1798
01:09:11,372 --> 01:09:13,142
It's a bit slippery as it's winter.

1799
01:09:14,782 --> 01:09:16,882
I get to see the view I only saw on TV.

1800
01:09:17,112 --> 01:09:19,181
- Be careful. - This is it, right, Dae Ho?

1801
01:09:19,182 --> 01:09:20,252
That's right.

1802
01:09:20,582 --> 01:09:22,681
- Here... - You should take a photo.

1803
01:09:22,682 --> 01:09:23,892
(Dae Ho's house doesn't feel unfamiliar.)

1804
01:09:24,322 --> 01:09:26,221
When else would we have a chance to take a photo together here?

1805
01:09:26,222 --> 01:09:27,222
Of course.

1806
01:09:27,692 --> 01:09:29,222
- Here. One... - It's cold.

1807
01:09:29,522 --> 01:09:31,462
One, two, three.

1808
01:09:32,762 --> 01:09:34,632
- Nice. - So they took a photo together.

1809
01:09:36,302 --> 01:09:38,372
We got it. Be careful going down.

1810
01:09:39,672 --> 01:09:41,141
(Sliding)

1811
01:09:41,142 --> 01:09:45,242
- Be careful. - Be careful.

1812
01:09:45,542 --> 01:09:46,581
You should watch out here.

1813
01:09:46,582 --> 01:09:47,582
(You must stay alert at all times here.)

1814
01:09:47,583 --> 01:09:49,242
- Be careful. - It's slippery.

1815
01:09:50,182 --> 01:09:52,311
Once you let your guard down here,

1816
01:09:52,312 --> 01:09:54,552
- you must call an ambulance. - Seriously.

1817
01:09:54,682 --> 01:09:55,981
Everywhere is life-threatening.

1818
01:09:55,982 --> 01:09:57,021
(Chuckling)

1819
01:09:57,022 --> 01:09:58,752
This is where I stay.

1820
01:09:59,762 --> 01:10:01,191
- Look at that. - It's...

1821
01:10:01,192 --> 01:10:02,222
- Oh, it's here? - Take a look around.

1822
01:10:02,262 --> 01:10:03,532
You live such a dynamic life.

1823
01:10:04,362 --> 01:10:06,432
Your mom must've been shocked.

1824
01:10:07,402 --> 01:10:09,161
I told you. Mom cried after seeing the place.

1825
01:10:09,162 --> 01:10:10,471
- For real? - It's quite clean...

1826
01:10:10,472 --> 01:10:11,772
compared to other days.

1827
01:10:11,832 --> 01:10:13,501
But it's quite clean.

1828
01:10:13,502 --> 01:10:15,141
- It's rather clean today. - Is that so?

1829
01:10:15,142 --> 01:10:16,201
Since my cousins were coming...

1830
01:10:16,202 --> 01:10:17,642
I cleaned it up.

1831
01:10:17,672 --> 01:10:18,672
Nana.

1832
01:10:18,842 --> 01:10:20,681
- Where is Nana? - There he is.

1833
01:10:20,682 --> 01:10:21,682
- It's my first time seeing him. - Nana.

1834
01:10:21,812 --> 01:10:23,582
Say hello. They're my cousins.

1835
01:10:23,982 --> 01:10:25,851
He must've eaten a lot.

1836
01:10:25,852 --> 01:10:26,951
- His belly is full. - Yes, it's full.

1837
01:10:26,952 --> 01:10:28,082
How cute.

1838
01:10:28,822 --> 01:10:30,121
All right. Now,

1839
01:10:30,122 --> 01:10:32,652
